Improved scheduling question:  
**“For every oven handoff and turkey-out cue, what hidden readiness, temperature recovery, resting, holding, pre-prep, or start-at-queue conditions must already be in place, not merely happen in the text in this order?”**

Answer and trigger revisions:  
The oven is the pacing device, not just a room with capacity. The turkey must rest before carving, but the oven still has a 35-minute stuffing bake, a 20-minute casserole bake, and an 8-minute roll warm after the turkey exits. The text says to bake stuffing “the moment the turkey is out,” yet it also requires a different oven temperature (`375°F`) after the turkey has been roasting at `325°F`; I added the hidden `recover-oven-to-375` step. I also revised side triggers so the oven transitions are gated by readiness: stuffing must be assembled before the stuffing bake starts; the green-bean casserole must be assembled before the casserole bake starts; gravy and potatoes start when the turkey comes out but are then held warm on burners. Because the green-bean and sauce prep cannot all wait until literally ten minutes after the turkey exits and still make the oven queue, the improved schedule moves trimming/slicing earlier and gates the actual blanching/sauce cooking to a ten-minute-after-turkey-out cue where practical. The final carry gate explicitly waits for the last oven cue, the final carve, the gravy holding step to start, and the potatoes holding step to start.

